  "decisions": [
    "Omnibox OnPaint inlines the base painter; intercept the actual PaintTextAndCursor call while the Omnibox painter owns the stack.",
    "Suppress only the engine caret visibility predicate during its actual UpdateCursorVisibility call. All other focus/model/accessibility queries retain application focus.",
    "Native pre-edit proposals execute original Views InsertChar/InsertText/DeleteRange transactions and veto the second native mutation.",
    "Actual NativeUI command selectors route cut/copy/paste to Omnibox ExecuteTextEditCommand, preserving application clipboard callbacks and paste sanitization.",
    "FocusManager receives modified native editing keys before browser accelerators; the owned native editor also precedes the retained address controller's command side effects. GNUstep resolves the commands without a copied key-binding table.",
    "Native eventfd invalidations schedule the actual Views paint callback; the adapter adds no caret timer.",
    "SelectionController OnMousePressed with handled=true retains real engine click-count/drag-threshold bookkeeping while bypassing engine text geometry.",
    "Native pointer selection enters the same actual NSTextField tracking loop used by Blink and Gecko; Views SetEditableSelectionRange applies the native range through real application callbacks.",
    "Held native tracking draws operation 5 snapshots without rebinding the busy editor. Canonical model, focus, enabled and size changes stop the old native gesture.",
    "Gesture ownership lasts until capture release/loss even after native tracking ends, preventing a late engine drag from using an uninitialized selection gesture.",
    "Actual release modifiers are retained; no synthetic modifier release is introduced at mouseUp."
  ],
  "open": [
    "Multiple-click metadata, right/middle buttons, selected-text data dragging, touch and long-field autoscroll",
    "Broader first-focus/unelision and selection-direction behavior",
    "Undo/redo command availability and native menu routing",
    "Clipboard availability when native and platform clipboard state differ",
    "IME/composition, selection direction, accessibility, scaling and long-field scrolling",
    "Remaining Views controls, menus, dialogs and detached menu layout",
    "Firefox address bar and frontends",
    "Chrome, Vivaldi and other derivative builds/frontends",
    "GTK, Qt/KDE and other foreign applications"
  ],
